# Third-party attribution

This project is derived from **UXAgent**, an open-source research system for
simulating usability testing with LLM agents:

  https://github.com/neuhai/UXAgent
  "UXAgent: A System for Simulating Usability Testing of Web Design with LLM"
  arXiv:2504.09407 — Yuxuan Lu, Bingsheng Yao, Hansu Gu, Jing Huang,
  Jessie Wang, Laurence Li, Haiyang Zhang, Qi He, Toby Jia-Jun Li, Dakuo Wang

The upstream project is MIT licensed. Substantial parts of the agent loop,
browser executor, and memory system originate there and are used under those
terms; the MIT licence requires this notice be retained in derivative works.

Work in this repository that is not from upstream — the audit and reporting
pipeline (Nielsen heuristic evaluation, evidence resolution, claim
verification, root-cause clustering, grounded task-completion outcome), the
Vue dashboard, and the deployment setup — is covered by the LICENSE file at
the repository root.
